  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-04-06T15:34:06.769Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "When using the ATOK IME (Input Method Editor) for Japanese input in VRChat, the Easy Anti-Cheat (EAC) system blocks the \"ATOK35DE.DLL\" file, making it impossible to type in Japanese. This issue occurs consistently and prevents users from communicating in Japanese within the game. Switching to another IME, such as Microsoft IME, may resolve the issue temporarily, but ATOK users face significant inconvenience due to this incompatibility.\n\nan IME is software commonly used in non-English speaking regions to input complex characters like kanji, hiragana, or katakana. In Japan, ATOK is a widely used alternative to Microsoft IME.\n\nHowever, EAC appears to misidentify certain DLLs associated with ATOK as potentially harmful or unapproved, leading to this problem.\n\nPlease investigate whether this is a false positive by EAC and consider allowing ATOK's DLLs to function properly within VRChat. This would enable Japanese users to communicate effectively without switching IMEs or encountering errors.\n\nIf additional details are needed, feel free to ask!",
